"Manage your reviews (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-reviews?language=en_US)\nciteturn1004search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 3 days ago; ## Manage your reviews ... Additionally, rating your audiobooks will help us continually provide relevant recommendations for you. ... You can see your audiobook reviews from the Audible desktop:\n\n## Manage your reviews\n\nYou can add, edit, and/or delete your reviews anytime. Writing reviews not only lets you express your opinion about an audiobook that you liked (or disliked), but it also helps other listeners decide if a title is right for them. Additionally, rating your audiobooks will help us continually provide relevant recommendations for you.\n\nNote: We don't tolerate comments that contain hate speech or harass, degrade, or intimidate others. If your review violates these or any of our other Review Guidelines, it may be removed.\n\n## How do I write a review of an Audible audiobook?\n\nOur customer reviews are a community forum that thrives on the participation of its members, united by their common passion for listening. So please note that:\n\n  * To leave a review or rate a title, you must have listened to at least 20% of it.\n  * It may take 2 business days to appear once approved.\n  * If the submitted review doesn't meet our guidelines, you'll be notified via email.\n\n\nIn the app\n\nFrom the player screen:\n\n  1. Open the player screen.\n  2. Select the 3-dot More menu at the top of the player.\n  3. Select Rate & Review.\n  4. Within the form, select the number of stars for the Overall, Performance, and Story.\n  5. Enter the title of your review.\n  6. Enter the review with a minimum of 15 words.\n  7. Select Submit.\n\nFrom your Library (using the 3-dot More menu):\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Locate the title you want to review.\n  4. Select the 3-dot More menu.\n  5. Select Rate & Review.\n  6. Within the form, select the number of stars for the Overall, Performance, and Story.\n  7. Enter the title of your review.\n  8. Enter the review with a minimum of 15 words.\n  9. Select Submit.\n\nFrom your Library (using select and hold):\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Locate the title you want to review.\n  4. Tap and hold on the title.\n  5. Select Rate & Review.\n  6. Within the form, select the number of stars for the Overall, Performance, and Story.\n  7. Enter the title of your review.\n  8. Enter the review with a minimum of 15 words.\n  9. Select Submit.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select the main menu.\n  3. Select Library.\n  4. Find the title you want to review.\n  5. Select the 3-dot More menu next to the title.\n  6. Select Rate & Review.\n  7. Within the form, select the number of stars for the following: Overall, Performance, Story.\n  8. Enter a headline for your review.\n  9. Enter the review (minimum of 15 words).\n  10. Select Preview.\n  11. Select Submit.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Find the title you want to review.\n  4. Select Write a review below the name of the narrator of the audiobook.\n  5. Within the form, select the number of stars for the following: Overall, Performance, Story.\n  6. Enter a headline for your review.\n  7. Enter the review (minimum of 15 words).\n  8. Select Preview.\n  9. Select Submit.\n\n## How do I edit my Audible review?\n\nIn the app\n\nFrom the player screen:\n\n  1. Open the player screen.\n  2. Select the 3-dot More menu at the top of the player.\n  3. Select Rate & Review.\n  4. Edit your review.\n  5. Select Submit.\n\nFrom your Library (using the 3-dot More menu):\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Locate the title you want to review.\n  4. Select the 3-dot More menu.\n  5. Select Rate & Review.\n  6. Edit your review.\n  7. Select Submit.\n\nFrom your Library (using select and hold):\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Locate the title you want to review.\n  4. Tap and hold on the title.\n  5. Select Rate & Review.\n  6. Edit your review.\n  7. Select Submit.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select the main menu.\n  3. Select Library.\n  4. Find the title you want to review.\n  5. Select the 3-dot More menu next to the title.\n  6. Select Edit review.\n  7. Edit your review\n  8. Select Preview.\n  9. Select Submit.\n\nOn desktop\n\nFrom your Library:\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Find the title you want to review.\n  4. Select Edit Review below the name of the narrator of the audiobook.\n  5. Edit your review\n  6. Select Preview.\n  7. Select Submit.\n\nFrom the Listener page:\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select your name on the top navigation.\n  3. Select Listener Page.\n  4. Find the review you want to edit.\n  5. Select Edit Review.\n  6. Edit your review\n  7. Select Preview.\n  8. Select Submit.\n\n## How do I delete my Audible review?\n\nDeleting reviews is currently only possible via the Audible website. If you're using the Audible app on a mobile device, you'll need to go to the Audible website via a mobile web browser and follow the steps below.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select the main menu.\n  3. Select Library.\n  4. Find the title you want to review.\n  5. Select the 3-dot More menu next to the title.\n  6. Select Edit review.\n  7. Select Delete review.\n  8. Select Delete review to confirm.\n\nOn desktop\n\nFrom your Library:\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Find the title you want to review.\n  4. Select Edit Review below the name of the narrator of the audiobook.\n  5. Select Delete review.\n  6. Select Delete review to confirm.\n\nFrom the Listener page:\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select your name on the top navigation.\n  3. Select Listener Page.\n  4. Find the review you want to edit.\n  5. Select Edit Review.\n  6. Select Delete review.\n  7. Select Delete review to confirm.\n\n## How do I see all my reviews?\n\nYou can see your audiobook reviews from the Audible desktop:\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select your name on the top navigation.\n  3. Select Listener Page.\n\n## How do I edit the name that shows on my reviews?\n\nFrom the Listener page\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select your name on the top navigation.\n  3. Select Listener Page.\n  4. Select Edit Profile.\n  5. Select Edit under the \"Your Listener Profile\" section.\n  6. Enter your Display Name, your location (optional), and language of preference.\n  7. Select Save.\n\nFrom the desktop settings\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select your name on the top navigation.\n  3. Select Membership details.\n  4. Select Settings.\n  5. Select Edit under the \"Your Listener Profile\" section.\n  6. Enter your Display Name, your location (optional), and language of preference.\n  7. Select Save.\n\nOn the mobile web settings \n\n  1. Select the main menu. \n  2. Select your name. \n  3. Select Settings. \n  4. Select Edit next to Your listener profile. \n  5. Enter your new display name. \n  6. Select Save. \n\nNote: The display name is optional and can be changed at any time.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManage your Wish List (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-wish-list?language=en_US)\nciteturn1004search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today; ## Manage your Wish List ... Keeping an organized and updated Audible Wish List will help you find your next listen faster and easier.\n\n## Manage your Wish List\n\nManage your Wish List\n\nKeeping an organized and updated Audible Wish List will help you find your next listen faster and easier. In this article, we'll cover the key aspects of Wish List management like how to view your Wish List, add new items, remove items, and shop directly from your Wish List.\n\nIn this article:\n\n  * Where is my Audible Wish List?\n  * How do I add titles to my Wish List?\n  * How do I remove a title from my Wish List?\n  * How do I buy a title from my Wish List?\n\n## Where is my Audible Wish List?\n\nYou can find and access your Wish List from the desktop and mobile site as well as from the Audible app.\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Select Lists.\n  4. Select Wish List.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select the main menu.\n  3. Select Wish List.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Wish List.\n\n\n## How do I add titles to my Wish List?\n\nYou can add titles to your wish list through multiple places.\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Search for the title you're interested in.\n  3. Select the title and go to its detail page.\n  4. Select Add to Wish List.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Search for the title you want.\n  3. Select More options.\n  4. Select Add to Wish List.\n\nOn desktop\n\nFrom search results:\n\n  1. Go to “Find your next great listen.”\n  2. Search for the title you want.\n  3. On the search results, select Add to Wish List next to the title you want.\n\nFrom the title’s detail page:\n\n  1. Go to “Find your next great listen.”\n  2. Search for the title you want.\n  3. Select the title you want.\n  4. Select Add to Wish List.\n\nFrom your cart\n\n  1. Go to your Cart\n  2. Locate the title you want in your Wish List.\n  3. Select Move to Wish List.\n\n\n## How do I remove a title from my Wish List?\n\nYou can remove titles from your wish list in several ways.\n\nIn the app\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Select Lists.\n  4. Select Wish List.\n  5. Select the 3-dots menu next to the title you want to remove.\n  6. Select Remove from Wish List.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Select the main menu.\n  2. Select Wish List.\n  3. Select the 3-dots menu next to the title you want to remove.\n  4. Select Remove from Wish List.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site.\n  2. Select Wish List.\n  3. Select Remove from Wish List next to the title you want to remove.\n\n## How do I buy a title from my Wish List?\n\nThere are multiple ways to buy or add titles from your wish list.\n\nIn the app\n\nUsing the 3-dots menu:\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Select Lists.\n  4. Select Wish List.\n  5. Select the 3-dots menu next to the title you want to purchase.\n  6. Select Title Details.\n  7. Choose a purchase option: Buy with 1 Credit or Buy for $X.XX.\n\nUsing select and hold:\n\n  1. Open the Audible app.\n  2. Select Library.\n  3. Select Lists.\n  4. Select Wish List.\n  5. Select and hold the title you want to purchase.\n  6. Select Title Details.\n  7. Choose a purchase option: Buy with 1 Credit or Buy for $X.XX.\n\nOn mobile web\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Select the main menu.\n  3. Select Wish List.\n  4. Select a title you'd like to purchase to go to its detail page.\n  5. Choose a payment option: Buy with 1 Credit or Buy for $X.XX.\n  6. Select Confirm purchase.\n\nOn desktop\n\n  1. Go to the Audible site and sign in.\n  2. Select Wish List in the site navigation.\n  3. Select Add to cart next to the title you want to purchase.\n  4. Select the Cart icon to be taken to the checkout page.\n  5. Select Go to checkout.\n  6. Select Confirm order.\n\nNotes:\n\n  * If you change your mind on a title, you can re-add it to your Wish List from the checkout page.\n  * After making your purchase, your title will be sent to your Library and you’ll get an email confirmation.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nView your Goodreads Want to Read shelf in the Audible app (https://help.audible.com/s/article/view-your-goodreads-want-to-read-list-in-audible?language=en_US)\nciteturn1004search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 2 days ago; Your Goodreads Want to Read shelf is now available directly in your Audible Library as a list, making it easy to discover audio versions of books you're interested in reading — all without switching between apps.\n\n## View your Goodreads Want to Read shelf in the Audible app\n\nYour Goodreads Want to Read shelf is now available directly in your Audible Library as a list, making it easy to discover audio versions of books you're interested in reading — all without switching between apps.\n\n## What is the Goodreads Want to Read shelf in Audible?\n\nWhen you connect your Goodreads and Amazon accounts, books from your Goodreads Want to Read shelf appear directly in a dedicated list in your Audible Library, within the Lists tab. You'll also see a view of this list as a carousel on the Listen Now tab.\n\n## How do I connect my Goodreads Want to Read shelf with my Audible account?\n\nConnect your Goodreads Want to Read shelf to your Amazon account by following the steps below.\n\nIn the Goodreads app:\n\n  1. Go to your Goodreads account settings.\n  2. Select Connect Amazon Account.\n  3. Select Allow.\n  4. Log in to your Goodreads account.\n\n## How do I view my Goodreads Want to Read shelf in the Audible app?\n\nTo view your Goodreads Want to Read shelf in your Audible account, follow these steps:\n\n  5. Go to your Library.\n  6. Select Lists in the top navigation (swipe left to view all sections).\n  7. Select Goodreads Want to Read.\n\nNote: You can also see Goodreads Want to Read shown as a carousel on the Listen Now tab in your Library.\n\n## Why don't I see my Goodreads Want to Read shelf in my Library?\n\nTo access your Goodreads Want to Read shelf in your Audible Library, you need an active Audible membership or trial and a Goodreads account that's connected to Amazon. After linking your accounts, please allow up to 24 hours for your Want to Read books to appear in your Library.\n\n## Why are some books missing from my Goodreads Want to Read shelf in the Audible app?\n\nOnly books that have audio versions available on Audible will appear in your Library. Books without audio versions or those not available on Audible won't be displayed. As we continue improving this feature, some titles with multiple editions may not match exactly between Goodreads and Audible, which means they might temporarily be unavailable in your Want to Read shelf on Audible. We're continuously enhancing this feature and working to improve accuracy over time.\n\n## How do I manage my Goodreads Want to Read shelf?\n\nTo add or remove books from your Goodreads Want to Read shelf, visit Goodreads directly. Any changes you make will automatically sync to your Audible Library.\n\n## How do I hide or remove my Goodreads Want to Read shelf from my Audible Library?\n\nYou can temporarily hide your Goodreads Want to Read shelf by following these steps:\n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. Select Connect to other apps.\n  4. Toggle off Goodreads integration.\n\nTo permanently remove your Goodreads books from Audible, unlink your Goodreads account via the Goodreads settings page. Please note that unlinking will disable all connected features between Goodreads and Audible, as well as between Goodreads and Amazon, including your Kindle account if you have one.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nListen with Alexa (https://help.audible.com/s/article/listen-with-alexa?language=en_US)\nciteturn1004search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today; By using voice commands, Alexa can help you add to your collection, find your next title, and listen at your own pace. ... ## Does the Alexa Voice Remote work with Audible on Fire TV?\n\n## Listen with Alexa\n\nYou can use Audible with any Alexa-enabled device, as well as in the Audible app for both iOS and Android. By using voice commands, Alexa can help you add to your collection, find your next title, and listen at your own pace.\n\nNote: To listen to your Audible titles, both Audible and the Alexa-enabled devices have to be connected to the same Amazon account (email).\n\nAlexa supports all Audible features except:\n\n  * Clips & bookmarks\n  * Rating & reviews\n  * Listening log\n  * Mark as finished\n\n## What are the voice commands for Audible on Alexa?\n\nYou can play Audible on Alexa by using the following voice commands, supported by most Alexa devices.\n\nNote: Because Alexa has access to a wide range of content, from music to TV shows, it helps to mention \"Audible\" and whether it's an audiobook or podcast when asking Alexa to play a title. That helps Alexa limit the title search to content in your Audible Library.\n\nTo do this...  | Say this\nListen to an audiobook  | \"Alexa, read my book.\" (plays your last book listened to); ␊\"Alexa, read [Tom Sawyer].\"; ␊\"Alexa, read [The Hobbit] from Audible.\"\nListen to Audible Stories  | \"Alexa, read me a story.\";\"Alexa, open Audible Stories.\";\"Alexa, read me a [nighttime] story.\"\nGo back or go forward  | \"Alexa, go back.\" (rewinds 30 seconds);\"Alexa, go forward.\" (fast forwards 30 seconds);\"Alexa, go back [45 seconds].\";\"Alexa, go forward [2 minutes].\"\nPause your audiobook  | \"Alexa, pause.\"\nResume your audiobook  | \"Alexa, resume.\"; \"Alexa, play.\"\nSkip chapters  | \"Alexa, next chapter.\";\"Alexa, previous chapter.\";\"Alexa, go to chapter number [7].\";\"Alexa, go to last chapter.\";\"Alexa, restart.\"\nSet a timer  | \"Alexa, stop reading in [12 minutes].\";Note: To set a timer, you must first ask Alexa to read your book, then use this command.\nAccess your Library  | \"Alexa, what are my audiobooks?\";\"Alexa, what's in my Audible library?\";\"Alexa, show my audiobooks.\";\"Alexa, list my Audible books.\";\"Alexa, list my audiobooks by [Jane Austen].\"\nSwitch profiles  | \"Alexa, switch profiles.\" (to access another Library);Note: Available if you have more than one profile set up through Amazon Family.\nPurchase books  | \"Alexa, buy [Name of Book].\";\"Alexa, read [Name of Book].\";Note: Audible members with credits available can purchase audiobooks using Alexa.\nUse Alexa as your personal assistant  | \"Alexa, who wrote Moby Dick?\"\nListen to a podcast  | \"Alexa, play my podcast.\" (plays your last podcast listened to);\"Alexa, play podcast [West Cork] from Audible.\";Note: This command isn't available in the Audible app for iOS.\nResume your podcast  | \"Alexa, resume [West Cork] podcast from Audible.\";Note: This command isn't available in the Audible app for iOS.\nPlay specific podcast episodes  | \"Alexa, next episode.\";\"Alexa, previous episode.\";\"Alexa, go to episode 5.\";\"Alexa, play episode 15 of the [West Cork] podcast.\";Note: This command isn't available in the Audible app for iOS.\n\n## How do I listen to Audible Stories with Alexa?\n\nYou can ask Alexa to read you free stories from any of our available genres using Audible Stories. Once a story is finished, you'll have the option to listen to another story in the same genre or you can ask for a different one. Say \"Alexa, read me a story\" or \"Alexa, open Audible Stories\" to view or hear the list of genres. Select or ask for the genre you're in the mood for.\n\nNote: By default, Alexa will remember where you left off. Just say \"Alexa, read me a story\" or \"Alexa, open Audible Stories\" again the next time you use it.\n\nAvailable genres\n\nYou can ask Alexa to play a short story from a specific genre. For example, try saying \"Alexa, read me a nighttime story.\"\n\n  * Nighttime\n  * Funny\n  * Scary\n  * Family\n  * Sci-Fi\n  * Fantasy\n  * Adventure\n  * Romance\n  * Feel-good\n  * Meditation\n  * Relaxation for sleep\n  * Random\n\n## How do I use Alexa in the Audible app?\n\nYou can use Alexa voice commands in the Audible app for both Android and iOS. To use Alexa, you must grand microphone access and Alexa must be toggled on in your app settings.\n\nNote: Even after Alexa is set to \"on,\" Alexa will only work if the Audible app is open. To protect your privacy, Alexa won't work if the screen is locked or you're interacting with another app—even if you're hearing Audible audio in the background.\n\n### Set up Alexa in the Audible app\n\n  1. Go to your Profile.\n  2. Select the Settings gear icon.\n  3. Select Alexa.\n  4. Toggle on Hands-free with Alexa.\n  5. A prompt will appear asking you to Agree and continue.\n  6. Another prompt will appear requesting microphone access.\n  7. Select Only while using the app or Always allow.\n  8. Say \"Alexa\" any time the app is on screen or select the Alexa icon in Car Mode, or assign Alexa to your playback controls in Player Settings > Customize.\n\nNote: At this time, the Audible app doesn't support Alexa voice commands for podcasts.\n\n## Can I play Audible podcasts using Alexa on my Echo Device?\n\nTo play a podcast on your Echo Show, Echo Dot, or other Echo device just say, \"Alexa, play the podcast [Name of podcast] from Audible\" and your podcast will start.\n\nTo continue your podcast where you left off on other devices, your Alexa device must be playing the podcast from Audible.\n\nNote: Alexa for the iOS and Android app does not yet support podcasts.\n\n## Can I listen to Audible in the Amazon Alexa app?\n\nThe Alexa App lets you set up and manage your Alexa-enabled devices. You can use the app to access your Audible Library in the Play tab, start playback in your app or on any of your linked devices, and use playback commands just like you would on an Echo Dot. Some supported playback controls include:\n\n  * Play/Pause\n  * Jump back 30 seconds\n  * Jump ahead 30 seconds\n  * Adjust volume\n  * Rewind/Fast forward\n  * Navigate chapters\n\n## Does the Alexa Voice Remote work with Audible on Fire TV?\n\nOnce the Audible app is downloaded, you can use your paired remote to access it on your Fire TV. You can skip forward and backward, play, and pause your audiobooks and podcasts. To use voice commands, press the microphone button on your Alexa Voice Remote.\n\nTry saying \"Alexa, play [Tom Sawyer] on Audible\" or \"Alexa, read my book.\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWish List (https://help.audible.com/s/topic/0TO4z000000SoJbGAK/wish-list?language=en_US)\nciteturn1004search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: today;   * Manage your Wish List\n\n# Wish List\n\nLearn how you can personalize this handy list found in your Library on the site and in the app.\n\n  * Manage your Wish List\n\n39561 Views•Sep 9, 2026•Knowledge--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAdministra tus reseñas (https://help.audible.com/s/article/manage-your-reviews?language=es_MX)\nciteturn1004search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; manage-your-reviews ... ## ¿Cómo escribo una reseña de un audiolibro de Audible?\n\n## Administra tus reseñas\n\n  * sep 3, 2026\n  * Knowledge\n\nTítulo\n\nAdministra tus reseñas\n\nNombre de URL\n\nmanage-your-reviews\n\nAnswer\n\nPuedes añadir, editar y/o eliminar tus reseñas en cualquier momento. Escribir reseñas no solo te permite expresar tu opinión sobre un audiolibro que te gustó (o no te gustó), sino que también ayuda a otros oyentes a decidir si un título es adecuado para ellos. Además, calificar tus audiolibros nos ayudará a proporcionarte continuamente recomendaciones relevantes.\nNota: No toleramos comentarios que contengan discursos de odio o que acosen, degraden o intimiden a otros. Si tu reseña infringue estas u otras de nuestras Normas de evaluación, podrá ser eliminada.\n\n## ¿Cómo escribo una reseña de un audiolibro de Audible?\n\nNuestras reseñas de clientes son un foro humano que se nutre de la participación de sus miembros, unidos por su pasión común por escuchar. Por favor, ten en cuenta que:\n\n  * Para dejar una reseña o calificar un título, debes haber escuchado al menos el 20% del mismo.\n  * Puede tardar 2 días hábiles en aparecer una vez aprobada.\n  * Si la reseña enviada no cumple con nuestras normas, serás notificado por correo electrónico.\n\nPuedes hacer una reseñar de los títulos que has escuchado a través de diferentes plataformas:\n\n### En la app\n\n  1. Ve a tu Biblioteca.\n  2. Selecciona el menú (3 puntos) junto al título.\n  3. Selecciona Calificar y reseñar.\n  4. Selecciona Dejar una reseña.\n  5. En el formulario, selecciona el número de estrellas para lo siguiente:\n    1. General\n    2. Interpretación\n    3. Historia\n  6. Ingresa tu reseña con un mínimo de 15 palabras.\n  7. Selecciona Enviar.\n\n### En web móvil\n\n  1. Selecciona el menú principal.\n  2. Selecciona Biblioteca.\n  3. Selecciona el menú desplegable junto al título que deseas reseñar.\n  4. Selecciona Calificar y reseñar.\n  5. En el formulario, selecciona el número de estrellas para lo siguiente:\n    1. General\n    2. Interpretación\n    3. Historia\n  6. Ingresa tu reseña con un mínimo de 15 palabras.\n  7. Selecciona Enviar.\n\n### En escritorio\n\n  1. Ve a tu Biblioteca.\n  2. Selecciona un título para ir a su página de detalles.\n  3. Selecciona Más opciones.\n  4. Selecciona Escribir una reseña.\n  5. En el formulario, selecciona el número de estrellas para lo siguiente:\n    1. General\n    2. Interpretación\n    3. Historia\n  6. Ingresa tu reseña con un mínimo de 15 palabras.\n  7. Selecciona Enviar.\n\n## ¿Cómo edito mi reseña de Audible?\n\n### En iOS\n\n  1. Selecciona Biblioteca.\n  2. Selecciona el menú desplegable (3 puntos) junto al título que deseas reseñar.\n  3. Selecciona Dejar o editar tu reseña.\n  4. Modifica la calificación de estrellas y/o la reseña escrita.\n  5. Selecciona Vista previa.\n  6. Selecciona Enviar.\n\n### En la app Android\n\n  1. Selecciona Biblioteca.\n  2. Selecciona el menú desplegable (3 puntos) junto al título que deseas reseñar.\n  3. Selecciona Calificar y Reseñar.\n  4. Modifica la calificación de estrellas y/o la reseña escrita.\n  5. Selecciona Enviar.\n\n### En web móvil\n\n  1. Selecciona el menú principal.\n  2. Selecciona Biblioteca.\n  3. Selecciona el menú desplegable (3 puntos) junto al título que deseas reseñar.\n  4. Selecciona Editar reseña.\n  5. Modifica la calificación de estrellas y/o la reseña escrita.\n  6. Selecciona Vista previa.\n  7. Selecciona Enviar.\n\n### En escritorio\n\n  1. En el sitio de escritorio, selecciona tu nombre en la navegación superior.\n  2. Selecciona Página de oyente o Calificaciones y reseñas.\n  3. Encuentra la reseña que deseas editar.\n  4. Selecciona Editar reseña.\n  5. Modifica la calificación de estrellas y/o la reseña escrita.\n  6. Selecciona Vista previa.\n  7. Selecciona Enviar.\n\n## ¿Cómo elimino mi reseña de Audible?\n\n### En web móvil\n\n  1. Selecciona el menú principal.\n  2. Selecciona Biblioteca.\n  3. Selecciona el menú desplegable (3 puntos) junto al título que deseas reseñar.\n  4. Selecciona Editar reseña.\n  5. Selecciona Eliminar reseña en la parte inferior de la pantalla.\n  6. Selecciona Eliminar reseña para confirmar.\n\n### En el sitio web de Audible\n\n  1. En el sitio de escritorio, selecciona tu nombre en la navegación superior.\n  2. Selecciona Página de oyente.\n  3. Encuentra la reseña que deseas eliminar.\n  4. Selecciona Editar reseña.\n  5. Selecciona Eliminar reseña.\n  6. Selecciona Eliminar reseña para confirmar.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSharing & reviews | Audible Help (https://help.audible.com/s/sharing-and-reviews?language=en_US)\nciteturn1004search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * Manage your reviews\n\n# Reviews & social sharing\n\nFind answers to common questions about writing reviews and sharing audiobook recommendations with friends over social media.\n\n  * Share a title\n\n269779 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge\n\n  * Manage your reviews\n\n46408 Views•Sep 3, 2026•Knowledge---------------------------------------------------------------------